  "note": "Mansa Musa's 1324 pilgrimage and the Cairo gold market.",
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "One man's giving broke a market",
      "steps": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Cairo, Egypt, the year 1324",
      "sub": "the king of Mali, Mansa Musa, arrives",
      "steps": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "He is walking to Makkah",
      "sub": "and giving gold away the whole way",
      "steps": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "So much that the price of gold sags",
      "steps": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "It took years to climb back",
      "steps": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "But the gold is not the story",
      "steps": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "He went home with scholars and jurists",
      "sub": "and an architect from Spain",
      "steps": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "And built Timbuktu into a city of books"
    },
    {
      "eyebrow": "Mansa Musa, Mali",
      "text": "The gold went back into vaults",
      "src": "Cairo chronicles; the Catalan Atlas, 1375"
    }
  ],
